@startuml UC-37 View Enrolled Classes List - Sequence Diagram (stereo)
skinparam defaultFontName "Segoe UI"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #000000
skinparam DatabaseBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #000000
skinparam ArrowColor #000000
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam maxMessageSize 280

actor Student
participant ":StudentClassResourcesPage" as UI <<user interaction>>
participant ":ClassController" as CTL <<coordinator>>
participant ":ClassManagementService" as SVC <<business logic>>
participant ":ClassRepository" as REPO <<interface>>
participant ":ClassMemberRepository" as MEM <<interface>>
database DB

autonumber
activate Student
Student ->> UI : Open the Enrolled Classes List from the main navigation
activate UI
UI ->> UI : loadClasses()
UI ->> CTL : GET /api/classes/enrolled?subject=&grade=&status=&q=&page=&size=
activate CTL
CTL ->> SVC : listEnrolledClasses(subject, grade, status, q, page, size)
activate SVC
SVC ->> SVC : take the signed-in student as the enrolled member
SVC ->> REPO : searchEnrolled(studentId, subject, grade, status, q, page, size)
activate REPO
REPO ->> DB : SELECT * FROM classes WHERE id IN the classes the student is ENROLLED in AND the selected filters ORDER BY updated_at DESC LIMIT ? OFFSET ?
activate DB
DB -->> REPO : rows
deactivate DB
REPO ->> DB : SELECT COUNT(*) FROM classes WHERE the same filters
activate DB
DB -->> REPO : total
deactivate DB
REPO -->> SVC : ClassRepository.SearchResult
deactivate REPO
SVC ->> MEM : countByClassId(classId)
activate MEM
MEM ->> DB : SELECT COUNT(*) FROM class_members WHERE class_id = ? AND status = 'ENROLLED'
activate DB
DB -->> MEM : enrolled count
deactivate DB
MEM -->> SVC : long
deactivate MEM
SVC ->> SVC : build one summary per enrolled class with its member count and status
SVC -->> CTL : ClassPage
deactivate SVC
CTL -->> UI : HTTP 200 + ClassPage
deactivate CTL

alt the student is enrolled in no class matching the filters
  UI -->> Student : Show MSG01 and no class card
else at least one enrolled class is found
  UI -->> Student : Show the enrolled class cards with name, subject, grade and Active / Inactive status
end

opt student searches or filters the list
  Student ->> UI : Enter a keyword or change the grade or subject filter
  UI ->> UI : rebuild the query parameters and reload the enrolled classes
  UI -->> Student : Refresh the list with the matching enrolled classes
end
deactivate UI
deactivate Student
@enduml
